    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if:  (a) an act is done for 2 or more reasons; and  (b) one of the reasons (whether or not it is the dominant or a substantial reason) is:  (i) the age of a person; or  (ii) a characteristic that appertains generally to persons of the age of a person; or  (iii) a characteristic that is generally imputed to persons of the age of a person."@en ;
