doc:sch-2-sec-31-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "31 Disability standards" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, formulate standards, to be known as disability standards, in relation to any area in which it is unlawful under this Part for a person to discriminate  Disability discrimination  Schedule 2 Amendments commencing 28 days after Royal Assent  Part 1  Disability Discrimination and Other Human Rights Legislation Amendment Act" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-2009-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2009 19"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-2009-5 ;
    values:originalText "against another person on the ground of a disability of the other person.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a disability standard may:  (a) deal with the following:  (i) reasonable adjustments;  (ii) strategies and programs to prevent harassment or victimisation of persons with a disability;  (iii) unjustifiable hardship;  (iv) exemptions from the disability standard, including the power (if any) of the Commission to grant such exemptions; or  (b) provide that the disability standard, in whole or in part, is or is not intended to affect the operation of a law of a State or Territory.  (3) Before making a disability standard, the Minister must take into consideration any comments made to the Minister by a Minister of a State or Territory who is responsible for matters relating to disability discrimination.  (4) A legislative instrument made under this section does not take effect before the end of the period in which it could be disallowed in either House of the Parliament." ;
    skos:definition "against another person on the ground of a disability of the other person.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a disability standard may:  (a) deal with the following:  (i) reasonable adjustments;  (ii) strategies and programs to prevent harassment or victimisation of persons with a disability;  (iii) unjustifiable hardship;  (iv) exemptions from the disability standard, including the power (if any) of the Commission to grant such exemptions; or  (b) provide that the disability standard, in whole or in part, is or is not intended to affect the operation of a law of a State or Territory.  (3) Before making a disability standard, the Minister must take into consideration any comments made to the Minister by a Minister of a State or Territory who is responsible for matters relating to disability discrimination.  (4) A legislative instrument made under this section does not take effect before the end of the period in which it could be disallowed in either House of the Parliament."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b721866f39d9e69948db2486167f3dabc84fd271ff3c6855ce12aee116960e2f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:disability-discrimination-and-other-human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2009-sch-2-sec-2009-5-ss-2 ;
